A||||24||kslish||Any open wheel race fans in the house?||||1||
Z||000000||kslish||04-16-2001||02:35 AM||||Even though I follow stock car racing, I've always been an open wheel fan at heart (CART, IRL, F1, etc.) but I have been in withdrawal as of late...<P>1.) Is Speedvision the only ones carrying F1 this year?  What happened to Fox Sports?  I don't get Speedvision in my area and watching 15 second highlights on RPM2night just sucks.<P>2.) Does anyone like Jason Priestly (from Beverly Hills 90210 fame) as a color commentator during ABC's telecasts of IRL races?  I'd like to give him a chance since he seems like he's genuinely interested in the sport, but something just doesn't seem right (in the same way Dennis Miller was a rough fit into Monday Night Football).  <P>3.) Does anyone really watch IRL races? (except for the Indy 500 of course)  I do, but it takes a backseat to CART with me if they are both on at the same time.<P>Just some things running through my mind after getting done with my taxes and seeing an advertisement for the new movie 'Driven' on TV.  I hope it's good, but a Stallone movie is usually hit or miss (I'm going to go see it reguardless).<P>Rambling on,<BR>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||04-16-2001||09:33 AM||||Ken, I usually watch IRL when a driver we've sponsored is driving and that's it. But that hasn't happened for like a year or 2 now, so I just go to the Indy. I still like it better than NASCAR by a ton, but it seems like NASCAR is always on, and IRL isn't.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||04-16-2001||09:56 AM||||well, coming from the heart of NASTYCAR country, i can tell you that i am looked at as some sort of stranger!  (and i was born and raised here!)<P>let me help youi with your questions:<BR>1) F1 is on speedvision only... for some reason they wound up with the rights to it, instead of sharing it like last year. (am i the only one that thought it was funy when Fox would say "the only live broadcast", while showing the San Marino Gran Prix at 2 pm EST?!)  personally, i did prefer Fox's coverage of the race... they had better comentator's.  i hate Sam Posey (do a search), Derek Bell is so much better!<P>2) Don't know who Jason Priestly is.  Here's a formula for you.. NASCAR+(Indylights+Indy 500)*ridiculous/Toney George=IRL<P>3) See abouve.  CART is much better, road racing is a true talent!  <P>I am also a big fan of sportscar racing, such as the American Le man's series.  In fact, I probably enjoy sportscar racing more than anything else.  The talent is more spread out, and generally, the cars are more equall, plus you have 3 classes of cars on the track at the same time!<P>Stallone movie looks interesting, not very realistic.<P>If you want to watch the best racing movie of all time, then tune into Speedvision on June 2nd... they are showing Le Mans, with Steve McQueen!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||04-16-2001||12:08 PM||||F-1 is on the net if you have streaming vid.<BR>try [The F1 links page] or [f1 news network].<BR>[ATLAS F-1] has all the latest news,interveiws, rumors,and a forum .<BR>for a great f-1 game-sim try GPL grand prix legends free down load at [Papyrus] site||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||04-16-2001||12:50 PM||||The IRL is surprisingly fun to watch.  It's kind of a guilty pleasure.  You know they're not as good as CART, but dammit, it's still fun.  Plus there are a few Americans to root for.  Seems like half of the best American CART racers can't find rides...they're either too young and no one wants to gamble on them, or they're too old and keep getting their butts kicked by guys from South America.  Where have you gone, Memo Gidley?<P>LeMans is great, and if you don't think so...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AW1955-t.gif">   <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||kslish||04-16-2001||01:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Ken, I usually watch IRL when a driver we've sponsored is driving and that's it. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just out of curiosity, who was the driver?  I've got all the Indy 500's for the past 10 or so years on tape.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>but it seems like NASCAR is always on, and IRL isn't.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That may be due to the fact that there is over 35 Winston Cup races a year compared to 13 for IRL and a little over 20 for CART.  If they add any more races to the NASCAR schedule they'll be racing well year round!<P>bHooper, I'll have to try the streaming video thing...to put my cable modem to the test and all.  I agree with you completely about CART and road racing.  I like the sheer speed of the bigger ovals but CART has a nice balance of the ovals and road/street tracks.  I'm going to try and make the Mid-Ohio race this year if possible.<P>I just checked out the rookie test stats at Indy and CART's Bruno Junqueira & Helio Castroneves posted the top times at almost 220 mph.  Looks like the CART teams are going to going to take it to the IRL again this year.  I'm actually beginning to enjoy the rivalry at the Indy 500 since CART left that part of the schedule open to let their teams compete and since Tony George is such a big-egoed s.o.b.  It was fun watching the look on his face as he awarded Montoya and car owner Chip Ganassi (a Pittsburgh native) the trophy last year.<P>Ken S.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||04-16-2001||04:02 PM||||Real race cars don't have fenders||||reg||1
