Z||000011||kslish||04-17-2001||08:00 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>kslish- Arie Luyendyk, but of course he just retired.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Did you know Arie is coming out of retirement for this year's Indy 500?  He's currently the oldest person registered for the race at 47 years old although Lyn St.James will beat that if she manages to find a ride for this year's race.  Never really liked Arie (he comes across as sort of arrogant sometimes) but I'm a big fan of St. James.  It was a shame Sara Fisher took her out in a wreck in last years 500. <P>Ken S.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric||04-17-2001||11:23 AM||||I don't like Sara Fisher.  In fact, she's the one who comes across arrogant, not Arie.  Arie just never really had the talent, so he made up for his lack of skills with crazy, wreckless driving.  He just reminds me of a skinny rich kid I grew up with.  That guy is just goofy as hell.  I thought it was so funny when AJ hit him in the face that one time on film.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||04-17-2001||12:27 PM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>I thought it was so funny when AJ hit him in the face that one time on film.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehe, I can't believe I almost forgot about that.<P>I don't have an opinion on Sara, only watched IRL like once, last Indy 500 so I haven't seen how she races.  I remember when she tangled with St. James at Indy, can't remember who was at fault if any.<P>I really believe St. James could win Indy. I hate to see her beg for sponsors every year and having to literally throw together a car and team to make the show, only then have something stupid go wrong during the race.<P>Other than Indy I don't really follow Cart or IRL open wheel racing much anymore.  Lost interest around when the leagues split up and after the loss of Scott Brayton.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
