Z||000015||Cheever2||04-17-2001||01:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR>Cheever... like the photo, mind if I borrow it?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Did you mean the McQueen photo posted by ChadMan?<P>I do agree that anything with lefts AND rights is better than watching ovals.  I'm only keeping up with IRL because of my hero, Eddie.  Missed the last broadcast and didn't catch Jason Priestly, was probably interesting.  Mostly I like F1 but don't have cable OR satellite right now, so I'm out of it.  <P>My favorite races are those on real city streets, especially Monte Carlo.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||AkursedX||04-17-2001||02:52 PM||||FORMULA ONE!!!  It's about the only racing I will watch, although I watch Nascar with my dad sometimes.  And I got a Satellite so I got Speedvision, hehehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <BR>I'm a Mika Hakkinen fan, I have been since back in the day when he was the #2 driver for the Lotus team!  Although he's doing crappy this year, I hope he picks it up.  I might have to start cheering for David Choultard (sp?)  I gotta stick with McClaren!  As much as I love Ferrari street cars, I can't stand Ferrari in Formula One.||||reg||14
Z||000017||ray b||04-17-2001||03:03 PM||||Sara fisher is real driver she got 2nd place<BR>at homestead race and at her age 19 is the best bet to move up to F-1 in future,  St james is slow old and in the way.<BR>arie did win at indy and drove in F-1 for lotus.no talent guys don't win indy. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||kslish||04-17-2001||03:44 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>Sara fisher is real driver she got 2nd place at homestead race and at her age 19 is the best bet to move up to F-1 in future,  St james is slow old and in the way.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I won't deny that Fisher has talent, but she has yet to develop the superhuman ability that great drivers have to sense what is going on around them at all times.  I seriously doubt she'll ever be in F1.  Lyn St. James is still the best female driver that I have ever seen as far as talent and skill.  If she was too old and slow she wouldn't have been trying to pass Fisher last year around the outside when Fisher did not realize that she was there and moved up in the groove putting them both into the wall. <P>I'll miss seeing F1 at Monte Carlo this year since I don't get Speedvision.  I'm sure it takes a brave soul to drive those narrow streets at those speeds and a even braver one to attempt a pass.  One mistake and your into the concrete barriers. <P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 04-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Shaft||04-17-2001||07:59 PM||||I don't really like IRL for the simple fact of how it came into existance. I don't like that Tony George feels he can try to force everyone in CART to join his series if they want to drive at Indy. I will say that I am a Sarah Fisher fan. She's from just south of Columbus and I love to see her show those IRL boys how to drive. CART rules all and Bobby Rahal is the man. I'm interested to see how this years  F1 season goes with him manning Jaguar Racing. Oh and Lisa, Arie is comming out of retirement, but i beleive it's just for the 500.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Eric||04-17-2001||08:21 PM||||Ray b, there's no way in hell Sara Fisher's going to F1.  I think she came up through sprint cars or gocarts not Indy Lights or Super V, am I right?  She doesn't have the skills or the God given talent to even drive CART, and you think they're going to let her go to F1.  Dude, put down the pipe.  <P>She's too old anyway.  Over in Europe, they breed F1 racers.  If you've ever seen competitive cart racing in Europe, you would realize a mediocre driver like Sara would not stand a snowball's chance.  The only way she could possibly get in an F1 race car would come in the form of a publicity stunt.  Because she's a woman we'll pony up the dough, and she can race with the big boys.  It probably wouldn't last long though.  Eventually the finacial backer would realize he's on a sinking ship, but it probably wouldn't even get that far.  She'd most likely die herself, or kill someone else on the track in the first race.  Remember Michael Andretti?  That man is one of the best CART racers of all time; nothing translates in F1.  Zenardi's back stateside agian.  Montoya is a fluke though.  He never should of had to prove himself in CART cars.  He's now a member of a winning team, and he'll do well.  But Sara won't!||||reg||1
Z||000021||bHooper||04-17-2001||10:08 PM||||now now, don't go a picking on the Andretti's!  when Michael went to F1, the cars had traction control, AWD, AWS, and hugly sophisticated launch programs.  all of this, and stupid Ron Dennis wouldn't even give him any practice time to learn the cars b4 the season began.<P>no one, i repeat NO ONE can go from one formula of racing to another with out testing, and be succesful!  (except for Mario)<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000022||ray b||04-17-2001||10:29 PM||||Go carts are way to F-1 senna, bros schumie and most others stated in go carts as kids.the best ever J M Fanigo stated in dirt stock cars in south am.<BR>sara fisher is only 19 and has time to move up cart first then F-1 ||||reg||1
Z||000023||ChadMan||04-17-2001||11:12 PM||||Why isn't America more interested in road racing?  <P>I keep waiting for the next Dan Gurney or Mario Andretti to come along, and it never happens.  Michael goes to F1 and gets his a$$ kicked.  Zanardi goes to F1 and gets HIS a$$ kicked.  If it weren't for Villeneuve (and soon Montoya), we'd have no pride at all.||||reg||5
Z||000024||Eric||04-18-2001||01:19 AM||||Villeneuve and Montoya aren't exactly homegrown either.  Like I said, the big money in the US is found in fendered cars.  I don't know why though.  There just aren't that many opportunities for youngsters to roadrace.  That's why most of the guys in CART have names you can't pronounce.  So why isn't America more interested in road racing?  Because there's not enough space to fit big-ass sponser logos on skinny little open wheel cars.<P>Sara Fisher has tested CART cars before.  I believe she did it like two years ago.  Don't you think they'd switch her over by now if she was so good.  I bet if they do anything, they'll just let her race ovals like she does now.  She's never been a roadracer and probably never will.  I don't think someone as small as her would have anything but a difficult time man-handling a 800 horsepower car around a hairpin.  Females by nature can't react as quickly as men.  They just aren't built for it.  Now you're talking about this little girl competing with men who probably have reaction times quicker than most fighter pilots.  There's just now freakin way, Rayb.  If she ever makes the move to CART, the results will not be pretty.  Never F1!<P>BHooper, traction control is coming back in Spain.  They also can use auto trannys.  I don't think it will hurt Montoya though.  For some reason I think he'll be the next Senna.  We'll see.<P>||||reg||1
